      shared set of execution ports and share an instruction cache, a data
      cache and an L2. All four cores share one L3 and the memory below it.
      Four workers are placed first one per core and then two to a core, and
      two bar charts compare the cost per byte and the instruction-cache miss
      rate of the two placements.
